{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>Take the Levites.</b> This was stated on the day the Tabernacle was erected, because in it are written the laws of the Levites — on that day they were needed for song. This pericope was written in order, and the two pericopes above it: in one it says 'bring near the tribe of Levi' etc., and in the other 'and I, behold, I have taken the Levites' — that is, to camp around the Tabernacle. After the Tabernacle was erected and the order of the standards and the kindling of the menorah, He commanded to appoint the Levites to serve it, and the pericope of the Levites was placed next to the pericope of the lamps, to say that the priests would be occupied with kindling the lamps and with the rest of the labors the Levites would assist them." "<b>From among the children of Israel.</b> For they had been intermingled beforehand."], :book :numbers, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:16:57.935618299Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}